abstract: Zhong dou jie fa (種痘捷法) is a Chinese vaccination pamphlet bearing an 1859
  imprint, published by 博濟醫局 (Boji Medical Institution) and attributed in the Bodleian
  catalogue to John Glasgow Kerr (J. G. Kerr). Its medical discourse, institutional
  imprint and physician’s signature provide material for studying the circulation
  of knowledge in Chinese and late Qing medical print culture. Version 0.2.1 transcribes
  nine original-print text faces across eight images of Bodleian Sinica 1240, providing
  TXT, JSON and TEI XML with references to the official source images. The text is
  a provisional AI transcription without human double collation or expert review.
  This revision applies 1 source-supported character correction following targeted
  non-blind review of reader proposals; it is not a new full-book independent collation.
